{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CBMZAnthroEmissions",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's anthropogenic gas emissions for the CBM-Z mechanism, `cbmz_addemiss_anthro` in chem/module_cbmz_addemiss.F (WRF v4.8.0), which emissions_driver calls for chem_opt = 170 (CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP) whenever an emission input is read (`emiss_inpt_opt > 0`). It is the gas half of the `emiss_opt = 4` (ecbmz_mosaic) package; the aerosol half is MosaicAnthroEmissions.\n\nThe scheme. Each emitted species is a molar flux E (mol km-2 hr-1, the `emis_ant` input field) into one emission layer (WRF puts the field for level k into layer k for k = 1..kemit; the reference configuration has kemit = 1, the surface layer), and its tendency is the flux over the layer's molar air column, `gas_layer_tendency` (WRF's `conv = 4.828e-4/rho_phy*dtstep/(dz8w*60.)`). This component is one emission layer; a consumer with kemit > 1 maps it over the layers. Fifteen CBM-Z species take their own field one for one: CSL, SO2, NO, ALD, HCHO, ORA2, NH3, ETH, CO, OL2, OLT, OLI, TOL, XYL, KET. The rest depend on which VARIETY of input was prepared, `emiss_inpt_opt`: a RADM2-variety input (1 or 102) is converted to CBM-Z paraffin carbon, PAR = 0.4 ALD + 2.9 HC3 + 4.8 HC5 + 7.9 HC8 + 0.9 KET + 2.8 OLI + 1.8 OLT + 1.0 ORA2, and nothing else; a CBM-Z-variety input (101, PNNL_CM) carries PAR in the E_HC5 field and also adds NO2, CH3OH and C2H5OH.\n\nWhat the scheme does that its comments do not say (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N116). (1) E_ISO is NEVER added for CBM-Z. The registry still describes the field as \"Anth+Bio for CBMZ\" -- it was added by `cbmz_addemiss_bio`, which was commented out in 2013 and replaced by `add_biogenics`, which does not read emis_ant -- so an inventory's anthropogenic isoprene is read in and discarded. (2) With a RADM2-variety input the emiss_opt = 4 package still reads E_NO2, E_CH3OH and E_C2H5OH, and they are discarded too: only the CBM-Z variety adds them. Both are reproduced here: no tendency is computed for isoprene, and the three are gated on the input variety. WRF also applies the same increment again for a DMS field under EMISS_INPT_PNNL_MAM, which chem_opt 170 does not carry and this component omits.\n\nThe increment WRF applies over a step is exactly dt times the tendency, since `conv` is proportional to dtstep: there is no operator-splitting error, so the observeds are the instantaneous rates a consumer adds.\n\nWhat the tests pin. Steps of the chem170 emissions capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_emis.sh: the reference column with emiss_opt = 4, bio_emiss_opt = 1 and synthetic hourly emission files), once per input variety, each asserting every tendency against the real64 replay of the dumped inputs through chem/module_cbmz_addemiss.F compiled unchanged (kernels/emissions_driver), at 1e-9 relative.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "emissions",
      "anthropogenic",
      "cbmz",
      "chem_opt-170"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0, chem/module_cbmz_addemiss.F (subroutine cbmz_addemiss_anthro), called from chem/emissions_driver.F for the CBM-Z chem_opt values."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R. A. and Peters, L. K. (1999). A new lumped structure photochemical mechanism for large-scale applications. J. Geophys. Res., 104(D23), 30387-30415."
      }
    ]
  },
